From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:56:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Drop a removed affiliated AP from the links of its stations

When an affiliated AP leaves the AP MLD through LINK_REMOVE,
hostapd_free_link_stas() frees the link stations of the non-AP MLDs
that stay associated over their other links. The stations on those
other links kept the removed link as valid, so STA output on the
control interface still listed it. hostapd_free_stas() of a BSS that is
not the association link of a non-AP MLD freed its link station with
ap_free_sta() and left the same stale link, for example on
DEAUTHENTICATE ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff on that BSS or on DISABLE of it.

Free each link station with ap_free_link_sta(), which also clears the
link on the other stations and frees the link station without
AP-STA-DISCONNECTED. Free the link stations of a BSS in
hostapd_free_stas() the same way, reported with
CTRL-EVENT-LINK-STA-REMOVED.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -620,6 +620,7 @@ void hostapd_free_stas(struct hostapd_da
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 	hostapd_free_mld_partner_stas(hapd);
+	hostapd_free_link_stas(hapd);
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	sta = hapd->sta_list;
@@ -693,10 +694,7 @@ void hostapd_free_link_stas(struct hosta
 			   MAC2STR(prev->addr));
 		ap_sta_link_event(hapd, WPA_EVENT_LINK_STA_REMOVED, prev->addr,
 				  hapd->mld_link_id);
-		/* The non-AP MLD stays associated over its other links, so no
-		 * disconnection is reported for it. */
-		ap_sta_set_authorized_flag(hapd, prev, 0);
-		ap_free_sta(hapd, prev);
+		ap_free_link_sta(hapd, prev);
 	}
 }
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
